{"files":[{"content":"#include <algorithm>\n#include <cstddef>\n#include <cstdint>\n#include <iostream>\n#include <utility>\n#include <vector>\n\nusing namespace std;\n\nstatic const int MOD = 1000000007;\n\nstatic int64_t modPower(int64_t value, int exponent) {\n    int64_t result = 1;\n    while (exponent > 0) {\n        if (exponent & 1) result = result * value % MOD;\n        value = value * value % MOD;\n        exponent >>= 1;\n    }\n    return result;\n}\n\nstatic int chooseWays(int total, int take, const vector<int>& factorial,\n                      const vector<int>& inverseFactorial) {\n    int64_t result = static_cast<int64_t>(factorial[total]) * inverseFactorial[take] % MOD;\n    result = result * inverseFactorial[total - take] % MOD;\n    return static_cast<int>(result);\n}\n\nint main() {\n    ios::sync_with_stdio(false);\n    cin.tie(nullptr);\n\n    int n, m;\n    if (!(cin >> n >> m)) return 0;\n\n    vector<pair<int, int>> blocked;\n    blocked.reserve(m);\n    for (int i = 0; i < m; ++i) {\n        int y, x;\n        cin >> y >> x;\n        blocked.emplace_back(y, x);\n    }\n    sort(blocked.begin(), blocked.end());\n    blocked.erase(unique(blocked.begin(), blocked.end()), blocked.end());\n\n    const pair<int, int> origin(0, 0);\n    const pair<int, int> destination(n - 1, n - 1);\n    if (binary_search(blocked.begin(), blocked.end(), origin) ||\n        binary_search(blocked.begin(), blocked.end(), destination)) {\n        cout << 0 << '\\n';\n        return 0;\n    }\n\n    const int maxFactorial = 2 * (n - 1);\n    vector<int> factorial(maxFactorial + 1, 1);\n    for (int i = 1; i <= maxFactorial; ++i) {\n        factorial[i] = static_cast<int>(static_cast<int64_t>(factorial[i - 1]) * i % MOD);\n    }\n    vector<int> inverseFactorial(maxFactorial + 1, 1);\n    inverseFactorial[maxFactorial] = static_cast<int>(modPower(factorial[maxFactorial], MOD - 2));\n    for (int i = maxFactorial; i > 0; --i) {\n        inverseFactorial[i - 1] = static_cast<int>(static_cast<int64_t>(inverseFactorial[i]) * i % MOD);\n    }\n\n    if (blocked.empty()) {\n        cout << chooseWays(maxFactorial, n - 1, factorial, inverseFactorial) << '\\n';\n        return 0;\n    }\n\n    if (blocked.size() <= static_cast<size_t>(n)) {\n        const int obstacleCount = static_cast<int>(blocked.size());\n        vector<int> firstHit(obstacleCount, 0);\n        constexpr int parallelReductionThreshold = 4096;\n\n        for (int i = 0; i < obstacleCount; ++i) {\n            const pair<int, int>& point = blocked[i];\n            long long sum = 0;\n            auto contribution = [&](int j) -> long long {\n                const pair<int, int>& prior = blocked[j];\n                if (prior.first > point.first || prior.second > point.second) return 0;\n                const int dx = point.second - prior.second;\n                const int dy = point.first - prior.first;\n                const int paths = chooseWays(dx + dy, dx, factorial, inverseFactorial);\n                return static_cast<int64_t>(firstHit[j]) * paths % MOD;\n            };\n\n            if (i < parallelReductionThreshold) {\n                for (int j = 0; j < i; ++j) {\n                    sum += contribution(j);\n                    if (sum >= MOD) sum -= MOD;\n                }\n            } else {\n#pragma omp parallel for schedule(static) reduction(+:sum)\n                for (int j = 0; j < i; ++j) {\n                    sum += contribution(j);\n                    sum %= MOD;\n                }\n            }\n\n            long long ways = chooseWays(point.first + point.second, point.first,\n                                        factorial, inverseFactorial) - sum % MOD;\n            if (ways < 0) ways += MOD;\n            firstHit[i] = static_cast<int>(ways);\n        }\n\n        long long answer = chooseWays(2 * (n - 1), n - 1, factorial, inverseFactorial);\n        long long blockedPaths = 0;\n        const pair<int, int> target(n - 1, n - 1);\n        auto contributionToTarget = [&](int j) -> long long {\n            const pair<int, int>& prior = blocked[j];\n            const int dx = target.second - prior.second;\n            const int dy = target.first - prior.first;\n            const int paths = chooseWays(dx + dy, dx, factorial, inverseFactorial);\n            return static_cast<int64_t>(firstHit[j]) * paths % MOD;\n        };\n        if (obstacleCount < parallelReductionThreshold) {\n            for (int j = 0; j < obstacleCount; ++j) {\n                blockedPaths += contributionToTarget(j);\n                if (blockedPaths >= MOD) blockedPaths -= MOD;\n            }\n        } else {\n#pragma omp parallel for schedule(static) reduction(+:blockedPaths)\n            for (int j = 0; j < obstacleCount; ++j) {\n                blockedPaths += contributionToTarget(j);\n                blockedPaths %= MOD;\n            }\n        }\n        answer -= blockedPaths % MOD;\n        if (answer < 0) answer += MOD;\n        cout << answer << '\\n';\n        return 0;\n    }\n\n    vector<size_t> rowOffsets(n + 1, 0);\n    for (const pair<int, int>& point : blocked) ++rowOffsets[point.first + 1];\n    for (int row = 1; row <= n; ++row) rowOffsets[row] += rowOffsets[row - 1];\n\n    vector<int> previousRow(n, 0);\n    vector<int> currentRow(n, 0);\n    size_t position = rowOffsets[0];\n    const size_t firstRowEnd = rowOffsets[1];\n    for (int column = 0; column < n; ++column) {\n        const bool isBlocked = position < firstRowEnd && blocked[position].second == column;\n        if (isBlocked) ++position;\n        if (isBlocked) {\n            previousRow[column] = 0;\n        } else if (column == 0) {\n            previousRow[column] = 1;\n        } else {\n            previousRow[column] = previousRow[column - 1];\n        }\n    }\n\n    if (n < 1024) {\n        for (int row = 1; row < n; ++row) {\n            position = rowOffsets[row];\n            const size_t rowEnd = rowOffsets[row + 1];\n            for (int column = 0; column < n; ++column) {\n                const bool isBlocked = position < rowEnd && blocked[position].second == column;\n                if (isBlocked) ++position;\n                if (isBlocked) {\n                    currentRow[column] = 0;\n                } else {\n                    int64_t value = previousRow[column];\n                    if (column > 0) value += currentRow[column - 1];\n                    currentRow[column] = static_cast<int>(value % MOD);\n                }\n            }\n            previousRow.swap(currentRow);\n        }\n    } else {\n        constexpr int chunkSize = 256;\n        const int chunkCount = (n + chunkSize - 1) / chunkSize;\n        vector<int> chunkTotal(chunkCount, 0);\n        vector<int> chunkSuffix(chunkCount, 0);\n        vector<int> chunkCarry(chunkCount, 0);\n        vector<unsigned char> chunkHasBlock(chunkCount, 0);\n        vector<size_t> chunkBlockBegin(chunkCount, 0);\n\n#pragma omp parallel\n        {\n            for (int row = 1; row < n; ++row) {\n                const size_t rowBegin = rowOffsets[row];\n                const size_t rowEnd = rowOffsets[row + 1];\n\n#pragma omp for schedule(static)\n                for (int chunk = 0; chunk < chunkCount; ++chunk) {\n                    const int firstColumn = chunk * chunkSize;\n                    const int endColumn = min(n, firstColumn + chunkSize);\n                    const auto beginIt = blocked.begin() + static_cast<ptrdiff_t>(rowBegin);\n                    const auto endIt = blocked.begin() + static_cast<ptrdiff_t>(rowEnd);\n                    const auto blockIt = lower_bound(beginIt, endIt, make_pair(row, firstColumn));\n                    size_t scan = static_cast<size_t>(blockIt - blocked.begin());\n                    chunkBlockBegin[chunk] = scan;\n\n                    int total = 0;\n                    int suffix = 0;\n                    bool sawBlock = false;\n                    for (int column = firstColumn; column < endColumn; ++column) {\n                        const bool isBlocked = scan < rowEnd && blocked[scan].second == column;\n                        if (isBlocked) {\n                            ++scan;\n                            sawBlock = true;\n                            suffix = 0;\n                        } else if (sawBlock) {\n                            suffix += previousRow[column];\n                            if (suffix >= MOD) suffix -= MOD;\n                        }\n                        total += previousRow[column];\n                        if (total >= MOD) total -= MOD;\n                    }\n                    chunkTotal[chunk] = total;\n                    chunkSuffix[chunk] = suffix;\n                    chunkHasBlock[chunk] = static_cast<unsigned char>(sawBlock);\n                }\n\n#pragma omp single\n                {\n                    int carry = 0;\n                    for (int chunk = 0; chunk < chunkCount; ++chunk) {\n                        chunkCarry[chunk] = carry;\n                        if (chunkHasBlock[chunk]) {\n                            carry = chunkSuffix[chunk];\n                        } else {\n                            carry += chunkTotal[chunk];\n                            if (carry >= MOD) carry -= MOD;\n                        }\n                    }\n                }\n\n#pragma omp for schedule(static)\n                for (int chunk = 0; chunk < chunkCount; ++chunk) {\n                    const int firstColumn = chunk * chunkSize;\n                    const int endColumn = min(n, firstColumn + chunkSize);\n                    size_t scan = chunkBlockBegin[chunk];\n                    int carry = chunkCarry[chunk];\n                    for (int column = firstColumn; column < endColumn; ++column) {\n                        const bool isBlocked = scan < rowEnd && blocked[scan].second == column;\n                        if (isBlocked) {\n                            ++scan;\n                            carry = 0;\n                            currentRow[column] = 0;\n                        } else {\n                            carry += previousRow[column];\n                            if (carry >= MOD) carry -= MOD;\n                            currentRow[column] = carry;\n                        }\n                    }\n                }\n\n#pragma omp single\n                {\n                    previousRow.swap(currentRow);\n                }\n            }\n        }\n    }\n\n    cout << previousRow[n - 1] << '\\n';\n    return 0;\n}\n","path":"src/solution.cpp"}],"hypothesis":"For sparse obstacles, a first-hit combinatorial recurrence reduces the grid DP to obstacle-pair work, with OpenMP reductions only once each predecessor sum is large enough to amortize team overhead. For denser obstacle sets, a linear-memory row DP uses statically shared chunks whose reset/suffix summaries preserve the row dependency while worksharing each row. This adaptive granularity should suit four CPU cores without allocating an N×N blocked grid.","notes":"No integration sources were declared. Crossover and OpenMP thresholds are hypotheses; this candidate was not measured here.","sources_kept":[],"transformations":["Replace the N×N blocked-cell structure with sorted, deduplicated obstacle coordinates and row offsets, keeping auxiliary memory linear in N plus the obstacle count.","Use factorial-based binomial counts and first-hit obstacle DP when the unique obstacle count is at most N; apply static OpenMP reductions to sufficiently long predecessor sums and to the final subtraction.","For denser cases, compute rolling rows; split each row into chunks with blocked-cell reset summaries, scan chunk carries, and statically workshare summary and output passes in a persistent OpenMP region.","Retain a serial rolling-row path for small dense grids to avoid parallel setup overhead."]}